        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.7.62",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.7.62",
      "verse": 62,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The children of Delaiah, the children of Tobiah, the children of Nekoda, six hundred and forty two.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.7.63",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.7.63",
      "verse": 63,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And of the priests: the children of Habaiah, the children of Koz, the children of Barzillai, who took ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the daughters of Barzillai the Gileadite for a wife, and was called after their name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.7.64",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.7.64",
      "verse": 64,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These sought their register ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "among",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " those that were reckoned by genealogy, but it was not found: therefore were they, as polluted, put from the priesthood.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.7.65",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.7.65",
      "verse": 65,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the Tirshatha said to them, that they should not eat of the most holy things, till there should stand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "up",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a priest with Urim and Thummim.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.7.66",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.7.66",
      "verse": 66,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The whole congregation together ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " forty two thousand three hundred and sixty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.7.67",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.7.67",
      "verse": 67,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Besides their man-servants and their maid-servants, of whom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " seven thousand three hundred and thirty seven: and they had two hundred and forty five singing-men and singing-women.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.7.68",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.7.68",
      "verse": 68,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their horses, seven hundred and thirty six: their mules, two hundred and forty five:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.7.69",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.7.69",
      "verse": 69,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " camels, four hundred and thirty five: six thousand seven hundred and twenty asses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.7.70",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.7.70",
      "verse": 70,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And some of the chief of the fathers gave to the work. The Tirshatha gave to the treasure a thousand drams of gold, fifty basins, five hundred and thirty priests' garments.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.7.71",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.7.71",
      "verse": 71,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "some",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the chief of the fathers gave to the treasure of the work, twenty thousand drams of gold, and two thousand and two hundred pounds of silver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.7.72",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.7.72",
      "verse": 72,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " which the rest of the people gave ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " twenty thousand drams of gold, and two thousand pounds of silver, and sixty seven priests' garments.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.7.73",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.7.73",
      "verse": 73,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So the priests, and the Levites, and the porters, and the singers, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "some",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the people, and the Nethinims, and all Israel, dwelt in their cities; and when the seventh month came, the children of Israel ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in their cities.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
